        "statement": "Assume the neutral pole-dipole equations adopted in [[post-rpm-mpd-truncation]] for the local moments of [[def-rpm-body-moments]]: along a $C^2$ future timelike proper-time curve $z$, with $U=dz/d\\tau$, $p$ future timelike and $S^{ab}=-S^{ba}$,\n$$D_\\tau p^a=-\\frac12R^a{}_{bcd}U^bS^{cd},\\qquad D_\\tau S^{ab}=p^aU^b-p^bU^a.$$\nFor any $C^1$ future unit observer field $n$ along the curve satisfying the SSC $S^{ab}n_b=0$, put $\\gamma=-g(n,U)/c>0$ and $E_n=-cg(p,n)$. Then\n$$c\\gamma p^a=\\frac{E_n}{c}U^a+S^{ab}D_\\tau n_b.$$\nIn the Pirani branch $n=U/c$, define $m=-g(p,U)/c^2>0$ and $a=D_\\tau U$; then\n$$p^a=mU^a+\\frac{1}{c^2}S^{ab}a_b.$$\nIn the parallel-observer (OKS) branch $D_\\tau n=0$, $p$ is a positive scalar multiple of $U$. In the TD branch $n=p/\\mu$, $\\mu=\\sqrt{-g(p,p)}$, the derivative term generally remains and the identity gives $mc^2p=\\mu^2U+S D_\\tau p$; it does not by itself imply $p\\parallel U$.",
