          "post-rpm-mpd-truncation": "physical-assumption",
          "pthm-rpm-td-invariants": "physical-result"
        },
        "statement": "Assume the neutral pole-dipole equations of [[post-rpm-mpd-truncation]] and the TD admissible region of [[pthm-rpm-td-invariants]]: $p$ is future timelike, $K$ is invertible, $W=K^{-1}p$ is future timelike, and the initial spin tensor satisfies $S^{ab}=0$. Then throughout the local solution the spin remains zero, $p$ is parallel transported, and\n$$U=\\frac{c}{\\mu}p,\\qquad \\mu=\\sqrt{-g(p,p)}=\\text{constant},\\qquad D_\\tau U=0.$$\nThus the representative curve is a timelike geodesic with constant rest mass $M=\\mu/c$ in this restricted branch.",
